  "content": {
    "id": "p35-q27",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "27",
    "prompt": "Find the first term that is greater than 100 in the sequence $3, 7, 11, \\ldots$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$103$, the $26$th term.",
      "worked": "$a=3$, $d=7-3=4$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}a_n&>100\\\\3+(n-1)4&>100\\\\3+4n-4&>100\\\\4n&>101\\\\n&>25.25\\end{aligned}$$\nThe least integer satisfying this is $n=26$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}a_{26}&=3+25(4)\\\\&=103\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
